From db0b3a0fa98cf09de326d9d2c22e2fb28ee6982b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:32:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Desktop sidebar: folded by default, and tighter when expanded

The rail is now the default on desktop: a browser that has not chosen
sees the 88px rail, and Expand is remembered ('0' in
aurelia.sidebar.rail). The expanded sidebar is tighter on desktop: 232px
instead of 260px, 44px rows at 15px instead of the drawer's 56px Figma
rows, and smaller gaps, logo row and New session button. NavItem and
SidebarContent take a compact prop that only the desktop aside passes,
so the phone drawer keeps its Figma measurements. --app-sidebar follows
(232px via data-sidebar='compact'). All of it behind
RELEASES.sidebarRail: production keeps the 260px sidebar.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Je1v64McNyB6XEu6gFgM4C
